{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":18935258,"ns":0,"title":"Doctrine","extract":"Doctrine (from Latin: doctrina, meaning 'teaching, instruction') is a codification of beliefs or a body of teachings or instructions, taught principles or positions, as the essence of teachings in a given branch of knowledge or in a belief system. The etymological Greek analogue is 'catechism'.","description":"Codification of beliefs","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}